# Compacted carbonate sediment thickness (m).
# Scientific colour map roma (Crameri), reversed so that thin sediment is blue and
# thick sediment brown, sampled one colour per class rather than by z: the classes
# below 50 m are 5 m wide and would otherwise share a single shade. Washed out with
# the recipe of the blue-orange-red pale variant it replaces - CIE LCh chroma x 0.45,
# lightness L -> 55 + 0.42 L - so the plate boundaries and coastlines drawn over it
# still read. NaN = 189/189/189, the continent grey. Generated 2026-09-15.
0	161/161/210	5	161/161/210
5	163/176/214	10	163/176/214
10	166/189/219	15	166/189/219
15	170/202/223	20	170/202/223
20	177/214/227	25	177/214/227
25	189/227/230	30	189/227/230
30	205/236/228	35	205/236/228
35	220/238/220	40	220/238/220
40	228/234/203	45	228/234/203
45	229/222/182	50	229/222/182
50	225/207/164	100	225/207/164
100	220/193/155	160	220/193/155
160	217/181/148	210	217/181/148
210	212/169/142	270	212/169/142
270	207/155/134	320	207/155/134
B	161/161/210
F	207/155/134
N	189/189/189
